   \[
   \left\langle \frac{\sqrt{2}}{d}(x - y), \frac{\sqrt{2}}{d}(z - y) \right\rangle = 0 \quad \text{for all } x, z \in S \text{ with } x \neq z
   \]

2. **Normalization Condition:**
   \[
   \left\| \frac{\sqrt{2}}{d}(x - y) \right\|^2 = 1 \implies \left\| x - y \right\|^2 = \frac{d^2}{2}
